{
  "_comment": [
    "The rules the plain-language checker applies. One list, read by three things:",
    "scripts/check.py on the command line, and two hooks in the plugin's hooks folder:",
    "stop-guard.py for chat replies, and file-guard.py for prose files. Add a rule here",
    "and all three apply it.",
    "",
    "Each rule names the clause it serves: '1' is ISO 24495-1:2023 and '3' is",
    "ISO 24495-3:2026. 'House style' rules come from the user, not from either standard.",
    "",
    "'block' findings make a hook send the text back for a rewrite, so a block rule has",
    "to be right nearly every time it fires. A rule that is often right but sometimes",
    "wrong is 'advise': the checker reports it, and the writer decides.",
    "",
    "Patterns are JavaScript regular expressions, matched case-insensitively unless a",
    "rule sets 'flags'. They run on prose only: code blocks, inline code, URLs and text",
    "inside double quotation marks are removed first. The Python checker reads them the",
    "same way, except for \\p{Extended_Pictographic}, which it replaces with a list of",
    "code points."
  ],
  "limits": {
    "sentenceWords": 25,
    "paragraphSentences": 5,
    "minSentenceVariation": 3.5,
    "variationNeedsSentences": 20,
    "headingWords": 10
  },
